Z||000021||Homicidal||08-01-2001||11:28 PM||||I'm a very big music fan, there isn't one style i don't like.  To prove it, here's a current mix CD i made for myself:<P>Burning Spear - Burning reggae<BR>Louis Armstrong - What A Wonderful World<BR>Reggie + The Full Effect - 11 - your boyfriend hates me<BR>Hey Mercedes - Bells<BR>11 - 311 - Uncalm<BR>98 Degrees - She's Out of My Life<BR>Boys 2 Men Yesterday (Acapella)<BR>Rocking Horse Winner - Atmosphere<BR>Burning Spear - New Experience<BR>98 Degrees - My Everything<BR>311 - Full Ride<BR>american football - Honestly?<BR>Missy Elliot - Get Ur Freak On (Duo Maxwell)<BR>o town - all or nothing<BR>Jimmy Eat World - 09 - Just Watch The Fireworks<BR>Travis - Why does it always rain on me?<BR>Blink 182 - Man Overboard<BR>Refused - Everlasting<BR>02 - 311 - Sick Tight<BR>Ludacris - Southern Hospitality (Feat Pha<BR>jimmy eat world - 05 - sweetness<P>Most of you probably won't know a few of those bands, but I suggest you try them out, especially:<P>Rocking Horse Winner<BR>Jimmy Eat World<BR>Saves The Day<BR>Dashboard Confessional<BR>The Anniversary<P>awesome music.  <P>I also love Techno for fast driving.  The Prodigy does this the best with songs like "Smack My *****  Up" and "Break + Enter".<P>------------------<BR><B>It's sad, in the 20th Century, in the 1990's, we would have to still go the same bullshit route<BR>that artists have to go, to get acceptance.  If it wasn't for the independence, if it wasn't for the <BR>small little cities, and the few little ghetto guys, trying to make music, it never would have happened.<BR>Some of these guys will never make a dime, some of thse guys will be poor and die, alone.  <P>But in the proccess, they've been the true renegades.<P>And the true rebels always walk alone anyways.</B>||||reg||10
